0118: stop hiding stages - stage 11 must not return on a negative result

0117 never ran. The level-12 log ended at "s11 cx branches did not wake
the core window", which is stage 11's own early return, so the cmd-db
census printed nothing at all - the second time in three patches that a
stage's failure path swallowed the next stage.

The rule is now unconditional: only the level guard may return. Stage 11
keeps its closing sequence inside the alive branch (bus buffers, AO
gating and the reset release are meaningless against a window that drops
writes) but a dead window no longer ends the boot, and "s11 done" prints
either way so the next stage is visibly reachable.
---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
index c7609a2..0316f10 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
@@ -1679,24 +1679,27 @@ sweet_gpu_probe(void)
         }
         printf("SWEET GPU: s11 core alive=%d\n", core != 0);
         if (!core) {
+                /* Same lesson as 0116, one stage later: a stage that returns on a
+                 * negative result hides every stage after it. Only the level
+                 * guard is allowed to return. */
                 printf("SWEET GPU: s11 cx branches did not wake the core window\n");
-                return;
+        } else {
+                /* Same closing sequence as stage 10, now against a window that can
+                 * hold a value: bus buffers, AO gating, reset release, and the
+                 * invalid-firmware code as the only expected result without
+                 * firmware. */
+                sweet_gpu_wr(gmu, SWEET_GMU_SYS_BUS_CONFIG, 1u);
+                printf("SWEET GMU: S11 SYS_BUS_CONFIG=%#x\n", sweet_gpu_rd(gmu, SWEET_GMU_SYS_BUS_CONFIG));
+                sweet_gpu_wr(gmu, SWEET_GMU_CGC_MODE_CNTL, 0x20202u);
+                printf("SWEET GMU: S11 CGC_MODE_CNTL=%#x\n", sweet_gpu_rd(gmu, SWEET_GMU_CGC_MODE_CNTL));
+                sweet_gpu_wr(gmu, SWEET_GMU_PWR_COL_CP_RESP, 0u);
+                sweet_gpu_wr(gmu, SWEET_GMU_CM3_SYSRESET, 0u);
+                delay(2000);
+                printf("SWEET GMU: S11 CM3_SYSRESET=%#x\n", sweet_gpu_rd(gmu, SWEET_GMU_CM3_SYSRESET));
+                printf("SWEET GMU: S11 CM3_FW_INIT_RESULT=%#x\n", sweet_gpu_rd(gmu, SWEET_GMU_CM3_FW_INIT_RESULT));
+                printf("SWEET GMU: S11 CM3_FW_BUSY=%#x\n", sweet_gpu_rd(gmu, SWEET_GMU_CM3_FW_BUSY));
+                printf("SWEET GMU: S11 HFI_VERSION_INFO=%#x\n", sweet_gpu_rd(gmu, SWEET_GMU_HFI_VERSION_INFO));
         }
